data.content:
# EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

## 1. `SetProperty` value parameter now requires a lambda expression

In EF Core 10, `SetProperty`'s value argument must be an `Expression<Func<TSource, TProperty>>` — a raw `Expression.Constant(...)` no longer works.

**Fix:** Wrap the value in a lambda:

```csharp
var sParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "s"); // unused but required
var blogParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b");

setters = Expression.Lambda<Func<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>, SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>>(
    Expression.Call(
        instance: setters.Body,
        methodName: nameof(SetPropertyCalls<Blog>.SetProperty),
        typeArguments: new[] { typeof(string) },
        arguments: new Expression[]
        {
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Property(blogParameter, nameof(Blog.Name)), blogParameter),
            // Wrap constant in a lambda: b => "foo"
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Constant("foo"), blogParameter)
        }),
    setters.Parameters);
```

---

## 2. Complex types — duplicate column names now error by default

EF Core 10 requires **explicit column names** when multiple complex properties share a CLR type (same `Street` property in two addresses). Previously columns were silently disambiguated; now you get a build-time error.

**Fix:** Configure column names explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, ab =>
    {
        ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingStreet");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ab =>
    {
        ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingStreet");
    });
});

// For nested complex types, same pattern:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pb =>
    {
        pb.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, ab =>
        {
            ab.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("Payment_BillingCity");
        });
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — signature changed

EF Core 10 consolidated the loose parameters into a `CommandEventData` object. The old per-parameter overload no longer exists.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        CommandEventData eventData)   // replaces commandId, connectionId, startTime
    {
        // Access old values via:
        //   eventData.CommandId
        //   eventData.ConnectionId
        //   eventData.StartTime
        /* logging */
    }
}
```

---

**Summary of action items:**

| Area | Change | Fix |
|------|--------|-----|
| `SetProperty` expressions | Value must be `Func<T,TProp>` lambda | Wrap constants in `Expression.Lambda` |
| Complex types | Shared CLR types error on duplicate columns | Add `HasColumnName()` per property |
| Diagnostics logger | Params rolled into `CommandEventData` | Update method signature |
